From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elkir0 <elkir0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] ARM: configs: gts28ltexx: the turbo test and soak
 fragments

gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config: the cpufreq test fragment (userspace
governor, cpufreq_dt a module loaded by hand, no modem driver) under its
own module tree, 6.12.114-turbo, for the GPU and A57 qualification from
RECOVERY in image mode.  gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config: the daily
gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config, unchanged, under the same module tree, for
the soak from RECOVERY on the persistent root, apart from the BOOT
kernel's lib/modules/6.12.114.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config | 45 +++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config | 49 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 94 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config
 create mode 100644 arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config

diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..07f3c2a5d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_soak.config
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+#
+# The turbo daily candidate, for its soak from RECOVERY on the persistent
+# root: gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config's lines below, unchanged, for the board
+# files that take the GPU to 700 MHz and the A57s to 1.5 GHz, and its own
+# module tree (LOCALVERSION at the end), apart from the BOOT kernel's
+# lib/modules/6.12.114. The BOOT kernel itself is built with
+# gts28ltexx_cpufreq.config.
+
+# --- gts28ltexx_modem.config ---
+# SPI core built in for the SS333 boot link; the controller, MIPI-LLI and
+# modem_v1 as modules that shannon-loader inserts (see that fragment).
+CONFIG_SPI=y
+CONFIG_SPI_S3C64XX=m
+CONFIG_MIPI_LLI=m
+CONFIG_SEC_MODEM_V1=m
+CONFIG_GPIO_SYSFS=y
+
+# --- CPU frequency scaling ---
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_STAT=y
+
+# schedutil by default: stage 1's idle run held the A53s at 400 MHz 95 % of
+# the time. userspace stays for cpufreq.sh's steps.
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_USERSPACE=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_PERFORMANCE=y
+
+# A module, as in the test kernels: udev loads it from the root, after the
+# initramfs's watchdog guard, so a fault in it cannot loop the boot.
+CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT=m
+
+# CPU cooling for the board's A53 maps.
+CONFIG_CPU_THERMAL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL=y
+
+# The soak's detectors (CPUFREQ.md section 9, 1f): a lockup or a hung task is
+# reported in the log. They only panic if their sysctls ask for it.
+CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
+
+# --- the soak's own module tree ---
+CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-turbo"
diff --git a/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..ce1b30a12
--- /dev/null
+++ b/arch/arm/configs/gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+#
+# GPU at 700 MHz and A57 scaling to 1.5 GHz, TEST kernels only (GPU.md
+# section 10 and CPUFREQ.md stage 2). Built from the cpufreq test fragment:
+# CPU frequency scaling, TEST kernels only (docs/hardware/CPUFREQ.md sections
+# 2.1 and 8.3 in the omarchy-tab-s2 repository).  Merged on top of
+# gts28ltexx_defconfig (kernel/kbuild-mainline.sh --fragment
+# gts28ltexx_turbo_test.config), for the board's
+# exynos5433-gts28ltexx-cpufreq.dtsi.  Takes the place of
+# gts28ltexx_modem.config: one fragment per build.
+
+# gts28ltexx_modem.config's lines without the modem drivers.  A test kernel
+# carries no modem module, so shannon-modem-prepare.service skips itself and
+# the CP never boots under a CPU being qualified: its boot programs eFuses
+# (CPUFREQ.md section 8.4).  SPI_S3C64XX only serves the modem's boot link.
+CONFIG_SPI=y
+CONFIG_GPIO_SYSFS=y
+
+# cpufreq core, with the transition table as the record of what ran.
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_STAT=y
+
+# userspace by default: loading the driver changes no clock and no rail.
+# The tests pin levels with scaling_setspeed; schedutil is for the soak.
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_DEFAULT_GOV_USERSPACE=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_USERSPACE=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_PERFORMANCE=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_GOV_SCHEDUTIL=y
+
+# A module, blacklisted at boot by t715.modblacklist=cpufreq_dt and loaded by
+# hand after the initramfs guard has run: built in, a bad table would hang
+# before it (the panfrost boot loop, CPUFREQ.md section 8.3).  Selects
+# CPUFREQ_DT_PLATDEV, built in, which creates the device it binds to.
+CONFIG_CPUFREQ_DT=m
+
+# CPU cooling: the cpufreq core registers each policy as a cooling device for
+# the board's maps.
+CONFIG_CPU_THERMAL=y
+CONFIG_CPU_FREQ_THERMAL=y
+
+# A hang must end in a panic, and the panic in a reset back to the daily
+# kernel (CPUFREQ.md section 8.3; the freeze of 2026-10-29).  The test script
+# sets the *_panic sysctls at load.
+CONFIG_DEBUG_KERNEL=y
+CONFIG_SOFTLOCKUP_DETECTOR=y
+CONFIG_DETECT_HUNG_TASK=y
+
+# Its own module tree, apart from the daily kernel's lib/modules/6.12.114.
+CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-turbo"
-- 
